u.lesson(
    "Konuşma sınavı stratejileri", "Konuşma sınavında cevaplarımı geliştirebilir (neden, örnek, karşı görüş, sonuç), doğal şekilde zaman kazanabilir, bilmediğim bir kelimeyi dolaylı anlatabilir ve kendimi düzeltebilirim.",
    {"kind": "dialogue", "title": "IELTS Konuşma Bölüm 3 tarzı soru", "lines": [
        {"speaker": "Examiner", "text": "Do you think that the government should invest more in public transport?"},
        {"speaker": "Candidate A", "text": "Yes. Public transport is good."},
        {"speaker": "Candidate B", "text": "That's an interesting question. On the whole, I'd say yes, for a couple of reasons. First of all, good public transport reduces traffic and pollution, which benefits everyone, not just the people who use it. In my city, for example, a new metro line opened a few years ago, and the difference in traffic has been quite noticeable. Having said that, I don't think investment alone is enough. If the service isn't reliable or affordable, people simply won't use it. So, in short, I'd support more investment, but only if it's well planned."}],
     "questions": [
        mc("Why is Candidate B's answer better?", ["It is longer and more developed, with reasons, an example and a counterpoint.", "It uses more difficult words only."], 0, "Geliştirilmiş cevap."),
        mc("What example does Candidate B give?", ["A new metro line in their city", "A bus strike", "A new airport"], 0, "\"a new metro line opened a few years ago\""),
     ]},
    {"explanation": "**IELTS Speaking** (3 bölüm, yaklaşık 11–14 dakika) ve **Cambridge C2 Proficiency Speaking** sınavında yüksek puan için **akıcılık, tutarlılık, kelime çeşitliliği, dilbilgisi çeşitliliği** ve **telaffuz** değerlendirilir.\n\n**1. Cevabı geliştirme formülü:**\n\n| Adım | Kalıp |\n|---|---|\n| **Doğrudan cevap** | *On the whole, I'd say yes / I'm not entirely convinced ...* |\n| **Neden** | *First of all, ... / The main reason is that ...* |\n| **Örnek** | *In my city, for example, ... / I remember when ...* |\n| **Karşı görüş** | *Having said that, ... / On the other hand, ...* |\n| **Sonuç** | *So, in short, ... / All things considered, ...* |\n\n**2. Zaman kazanma (doğal yollarla):**\n\n- *That's an interesting question.*\n- *That's not something I've thought about much, but ...*\n- *Let me think about that for a moment.*\n- *Well, it depends on what you mean by ...*\n\n**Dikkat:** Bu ifadeleri **her soruda** kullanmayın; yapay görünür.\n\n**3. Dolaylı anlatım (circumlocution):** Bir kelimeyi unuttuğunuzda **durmayın**, açıklayın:\n\n- *It's a kind of ... / It's the thing you use to ...*\n- *I can't think of the exact word, but it's similar to ...*\n- *It's the opposite of ...*\n\n**4. Kendini düzeltme (self-correction):** Doğal ve olumludur.\n\n- *He go... sorry, he went to ...*\n- *... or rather, ... / What I mean is ...*\n\n**5. C2 seviyesinde puan getiren özellikler:**\n\n- **Temkinli dil:** *I'd say, It seems to me, to some extent*\n- **Deyimler** (doğal ve az): *a double-edged sword, the tip of the iceberg*\n- **Çeşitli yapılar:** cleft (*What worries me is ...*), şart (*Were the government to ...*), devrik yapı (ölçülü)\n- **Kesin kelimeler:** *noticeable, affordable, reliable*\n\n**Kaçının:** Ezberlenmiş uzun kalıplar, çok kısa cevaplar, aynı bağlaçların tekrarı (*and ... and ...*).",
     "examples": [{"en": "That's not something I've thought about much, but I'd say ...", "tr": "Bu pek düşündüğüm bir şey değil ama ... diyebilirim."},
                  {"en": "I can't think of the exact word, but it's a kind of tool for ...", "tr": "Tam kelimeyi hatırlayamıyorum ama ... için kullanılan bir tür alet."},
                  {"en": "What worries me most is the cost.", "tr": "Beni en çok endişelendiren maliyet."}],
     "turkishNote": "Türk öğrenciler konuşma sınavlarında genellikle iki hata yapar: Ya çok kısa cevap verir (\"Yes, I think so\") ya da önceden ezberlenmiş uzun paragrafları tekrarlar. Sınav görevlisi her ikisini de fark eder. En iyi strateji, \"Cevap + Neden + Örnek + Karşı görüş + Sonuç\" yapısını içselleştirmektir. Ayrıca bir kelimeyi unuttuğunuzda Türkçe düşünüp susmak yerine, kelimeyi İngilizce olarak dolaylı anlatmak akıcılık puanınızı korur."},
    [
        mc("Daha yüksek puan alacak cevap:", ["Yes, it's good.", "On the whole, yes. The main reason is ... For example, ... Having said that, ..."], 1, "Geliştirilmiş cevap."),
        mc("Bir kelimeyi unuttuğunuzda:", ["Uzun süre susun.", "Kelimeyi dolaylı anlatın: \"It's a kind of ...\""], 1, "Circumlocution."),
        mc("Zaman kazanma ifadeleri:", ["Her soruda kullanılmalı.", "Ara sıra ve doğal kullanılmalı."], 1, "Ölçü."),
        mc("Karşı görüş eklemek için:", ["Having said that, ...", "First of all, ..."], 0, "Counterpoint."),
        gap("That's an ___ question. Let me think. (ilginç)", ["interesting"], "That's an interesting question."),
        gap("Having ___ that, I don't think it's the only solution.", ["said"], "Having said that."),
        gap("I can't think of the exact ___, but it's similar to a ladder.", ["word"], "the exact word."),
        gap("All things ___, I'd support the idea. (göz önüne alındığında)", ["considered"], "All things considered."),
        listen("Examiner: Is it important for children to learn a second language? Candidate: Absolutely, though perhaps not for the reasons people usually give. Of course, it helps with future jobs, but what I find more important is that it teaches children that there's more than one way of seeing the world. My niece, for instance, started learning Spanish at seven, and she's become much more curious about other cultures. That said, I don't think it should be forced on children who are struggling with their first language.", "Aday hangi geliştirme adımlarını kullanıyor?", ["Sadece doğrudan cevap", "Cevap, neden, örnek ve karşı görüş", "Sadece bir örnek"], 1, "Absolutely + what I find more important + My niece + That said."),
        match([("That's an interesting question.", "zaman kazanmak"), ("It's a kind of ...", "dolaylı anlatım"), ("Having said that, ...", "karşı görüş"), ("In my city, for example, ...", "örnek"), ("All things considered, ...", "sonuç")], "Her ifadeyi işleviyle eşleştirin."),
    ],
    {"kind": "speaking", "task": speak("Aşağıdaki IELTS Bölüm 3 / CPE tarzı sorulardan ikisine, her biri en az 45 saniye olacak şekilde cevap verin. \"Cevap + Neden + Örnek + Karşı görüş + Sonuç\" yapısını kullanın, en az bir C2 yapısı (cleft, inversion, mixed conditional) ve temkinli dil ekleyin: (1) Do you think social media has made people more or less connected? (2) Should university education be free for everyone? (3) How might cities change in the next fifty years?",
                                       "One: That's a really interesting question. I'd say that, paradoxically, social media has made us both more and less connected. On the one hand, it's never been easier to stay in touch with friends and family who live far away. My cousin, for instance, lives in Canada, and we talk almost every day thanks to messaging apps. Having said that, what worries me is that many people now spend more time scrolling than actually talking to the people around them. So, all things considered, I think it depends on how we use it. Three: Well, it's hard to say exactly, but I suspect cities will look very different. If current trends continue, we'll probably see far fewer private cars and much more green space. Were governments to invest seriously in renewable energy, cities could also become much cleaner. On the other hand, rising populations may put enormous pressure on housing. In short, I think cities will be greener, but perhaps also more crowded.",
                                       ["Geliştirilmiş cevaplar", "Neden, örnek, karşı görüş, sonuç", "C2 yapıları", "Temkinli dil ve akıcılık"])},
)

