u.lesson(
    "Deneme: iki metni özetle ve değerlendir", "Cambridge C2 Proficiency Writing Part 1 tarzında, iki kısa metnin ana fikirlerini kendi sözlerimle özetleyip değerlendiren ve kendi görüşümü ekleyen yüksek puanlı bir deneme yazabilirim.",
    {"kind": "text", "title": "Örnek görev", "body": "Read the two texts below. Write an essay summarising and evaluating the key points from both texts. Use your own words throughout as far as possible, and include your own ideas in your answer. (240–280 words)\n\nText 1:\n\"Tourism brings undeniable economic benefits to local communities. It creates jobs, supports small businesses and often funds the preservation of historic sites that might otherwise fall into ruin. For many regions, it is quite simply the main source of income.\"\n\nText 2:\n\"Mass tourism can do lasting damage to the very places it claims to celebrate. Popular destinations become overcrowded, local residents are priced out of their own neighbourhoods, and fragile ecosystems are put under severe pressure. The economic gains are rarely shared fairly.\"",
     "questions": [
        mc("What must you do in this task?", ["Only give your opinion", "Summarise and evaluate both texts, and include your own ideas", "Copy the key sentences from the texts"], 1, "\"summarising and evaluating ... include your own ideas\""),
        mc("What is the main point of Text 2?", ["Tourism creates jobs.", "Mass tourism can harm places and people.", "Tourism should be banned."], 1, "\"can do lasting damage\""),
     ]},
    {"explanation": "**Cambridge C2 Proficiency Writing Part 1:** İki kısa metnin **ana noktalarını özetleyip değerlendiren** zorunlu bir deneme (240–280 kelime). Bu görev, C2 Ünite 3'teki (akademik yazı) **yeniden ifade** ve **sentez** becerilerini gerektirir.\n\n**Değerlendirme ölçütleri:** İçerik (her iki metnin ana noktaları), iletişimsel başarı (uygun üslup ve okuyucu etkisi), organizasyon ve dil.\n\n**Önerilen yapı (4 paragraf):**\n\n| Paragraf | İçerik |\n|---|---|\n| **1. Giriş** | Konuyu tanıt; iki metnin genel olarak **farklı / benzer** bakış açılarını belirt |\n| **2. Metin 1** | Ana noktaları **kendi sözlerinle** özetle + **değerlendir** (katılıyor musun? ne kadar ikna edici?) |\n| **3. Metin 2** | Ana noktaları **kendi sözlerinle** özetle + **değerlendir** |\n| **4. Sonuç** | Kendi **net görüşünü** belirt; iki metni **sentezle** |\n\n**Değerlendirme kalıpları:**\n\n- *The first text makes a compelling case for ...*\n- *While this argument has some merit, it overlooks ...*\n- *The writer of the second text rightly points out that ...*\n- *This view is, in my opinion, somewhat one-sided / overstated.*\n- *Both texts, however, fail to consider ...*\n- *A more balanced view would be that ...*\n\n**Yeniden ifade (paraphrase) zorunlu!**\n\n| Metindeki ifade | Kendi sözlerinizle |\n|---|---|\n| *undeniable economic benefits* | *clear financial advantages* |\n| *fall into ruin* | *be neglected / deteriorate* |\n| *priced out of their own neighbourhoods* | *can no longer afford to live in the areas where they grew up* |\n| *fragile ecosystems* | *vulnerable natural environments* |\n\n**Sık yapılan hatalar:**\n\n1. Metinlerden **cümleleri kopyalamak** (puan kaybı)\n2. Sadece **özetleyip değerlendirmemek**\n3. Bir metni **atlamak**\n4. **Kendi görüşünü** eklememek\n5. **Kelime sınırını** aşmak ya da altında kalmak\n\n**Zaman yönetimi:** Planlama (5–10 dk) → Yazma (25–30 dk) → Gözden geçirme (5 dk).",
     "examples": [{"en": "The first text makes a compelling case for the economic value of tourism.", "tr": "İlk metin turizmin ekonomik değeri için ikna edici bir savunma yapıyor."},
                  {"en": "While this argument has some merit, it overlooks the social cost.", "tr": "Bu argümanın bazı haklı yönleri olsa da sosyal maliyeti göz ardı ediyor."},
                  {"en": "A more balanced view would be that tourism must be carefully managed.", "tr": "Daha dengeli bir görüş, turizmin dikkatle yönetilmesi gerektiği olurdu."}],
     "turkishNote": "Türk öğrenciler bu görevde genellikle iki hata yapar: Metinlerden cümleleri neredeyse aynen kopyalar (Ünite 3'teki \"patchwriting\") ve özetlemekle yetinip değerlendirme yapmaz. Sınav görevlisi sizin metinleri anlayıp anlamadığınızı değil, onları kendi sözlerinizle yeniden ifade edip eleştirel bir şekilde değerlendirip değerlendiremediğinizi ölçer. Her metin için şu soruyu sorun: \"Bu argüman ne kadar güçlü? Neyi göz ardı ediyor?\" Son paragrafta mutlaka kendi net görüşünüzü belirtin."},
    [
        mc("Bu görevde metinlerden cümle kopyalamak:", ["Puan getirir.", "Puan kaybettirir."], 1, "Paraphrase."),
        mc("Değerlendirme cümlesi:", ["Text 1 says tourism creates jobs.", "While this argument has some merit, it overlooks the social cost."], 1, "Evaluation."),
        mc("Kendi görüşünüz nerede en açık olmalı?", ["Sonuç paragrafında", "Hiçbir yerde"], 0, "Sonuç."),
        mc("\"priced out of their own neighbourhoods\" için iyi bir yeniden ifade:", ["priced out of their neighbourhoods", "unable to afford to live in the areas where they grew up"], 1, "Paraphrase."),
        gap("The first text makes a ___ case for tourism. (ikna edici)", ["compelling", "convincing", "strong", "persuasive"], "compelling case."),
        gap("While this argument has some ___, it is rather one-sided. (haklılık payı)", ["merit", "validity"], "has some merit."),
        gap("The writer rightly ___ out that ecosystems are fragile.", ["points"], "points out."),
        gap("Both texts, however, fail to ___ the role of local governments. (göz önüne almak)", ["consider", "mention", "address"], "fail to consider."),
        listen("When you write the summary-and-evaluation essay, don't simply say \"Text 1 says this, Text 2 says that.\" The examiner wants to see you weigh the arguments. Ask yourself: which text is more convincing, and why? What does each writer leave out? Then make your own position clear at the end.", "Sınav görevlisi bu denemede ne görmek istiyor?", ["Sadece iki metnin özeti", "Argümanların tartılması ve yazarın kendi net görüşü", "Metinlerden doğrudan alıntılar"], 1, "\"weigh the arguments ... make your own position clear\""),
        typ("Kendi sözlerinizle ifade edin: \"fragile ecosystems are put under severe pressure\" (vulnerable natural environments ...)", variants("vulnerable natural environments are seriously threatened", "vulnerable natural environments are under serious threat", "vulnerable natural environments are badly damaged", "vulnerable natural environments come under great strain", "vulnerable natural environments are placed under great strain", "vulnerable natural environments suffer considerable harm"), "vulnerable natural environments are seriously threatened"),
    ],
    {"kind": "writing", "task": write("Ders metnindeki iki turizm metnini okuyun ve bir deneme yazın (240–280 kelime): Her iki metnin ana noktalarını mümkün olduğunca kendi sözlerinizle özetleyin ve değerlendirin, ve kendi görüşünüzü ekleyin. Dört paragraflık yapıyı ve değerlendirme kalıplarını kullanın; metinlerden cümle kopyalamayın.",
                                      "Tourism is often presented as either a blessing or a curse for the places that receive visitors. The two texts take markedly different positions on this issue, focusing respectively on its financial advantages and its social and environmental costs.\n\nThe first text argues that tourism offers clear economic benefits. It generates employment, helps local enterprises to survive and frequently provides the money needed to protect historic buildings that would otherwise deteriorate. For some areas, the writer claims, visitors are the most important source of revenue. This argument is undoubtedly persuasive, particularly in relation to rural or economically isolated regions. However, it presents tourism in an entirely positive light and makes no mention of who actually receives the profits.\n\nThe second text, by contrast, focuses on the harm caused by large numbers of visitors. The writer rightly points out that popular places can become unbearably crowded, that rising property prices may force local people to leave the areas where they grew up, and that vulnerable natural environments can suffer considerable damage. The claim that the profits are seldom distributed fairly is, in my view, the most important point in either text, although the writer arguably overstates the case by implying that the costs always outweigh the benefits.\n\nIn my opinion, both texts contain some truth, but neither offers a complete picture. Tourism is neither inherently good nor inherently harmful; its impact depends largely on how it is managed. Measures such as limiting visitor numbers, investing tourist taxes in local housing and protecting sensitive natural areas could allow communities to enjoy the economic advantages without paying such a high social and environmental price.",
                                      ["Her iki metnin ana noktaları", "Kendi sözleriyle ifade (kopyalama yok)", "Eleştirel değerlendirme", "Net kendi görüşü", "Yapı, üslup ve kelime sınırı"])},
)

u.test([
    mc("I'm sure he didn't see us. CAN'T → He ___ us.", ["can't have seen", "can't see"], 0, "Modal perfect"),
    mc("Anahtar kelimeli dönüşümde verilen kelime:", ["Değiştirilebilir.", "Asla değiştirilmez."], 1, "Kural"),
    mc("The new policy has ___ rise to criticism.", ["given", "made"], 0, "give rise to"),
    mc("Yazarın tutumu \"sceptical\":", ["Şüpheci", "Coşkulu"], 0, "sceptical"),
    mc("Konuşma sınavında bir kelimeyi unutunca:", ["Susun.", "Dolaylı anlatın."], 1, "Circumlocution"),
    gap("As soon as I arrived, it started to rain. SOONER → No sooner ___ I arrived than it started to rain.", ["had"], "No sooner had I"),
    gap("People say that the house is haunted. SAID → The house is ___ to be haunted.", ["said"], "Passive reporting"),
    gap("Although he tried hard, he failed. HOWEVER → ___ hard he tried, he failed.", ["However"], "However + zarf"),
    gap("In the long ___, the plan will save money.", ["run"], "in the long run"),
    gap("There is no proof ___ that he was there. (hiçbir)", ["whatsoever"], "whatsoever"),
    gap("What can be ___ from the last paragraph? (çıkarım)", ["inferred"], "inferred"),
    gap("Having ___ that, I don't think it will work.", ["said"], "Having said that"),
    listen("When answering reading questions, always look for evidence in the text. If you can't point to a specific word or sentence that supports your answer, it's probably wrong. And be careful with options that repeat words from the text exactly; they're often distractors.", "Bu tavsiyeye göre metindeki kelimeleri aynen tekrarlayan seçenekler:", ["Her zaman doğrudur.", "Genellikle çeldiricidir."], 1, "Distractors."),
    typ("Dönüştürün (BEEN): \"If you hadn't helped me, I would have failed.\" → Had it ___, I would have failed.", variants("not been for your help", "not been for you", "not been for your assistance"), "not been for your help"),
    write("Aşağıdaki iki metni okuyun ve bir deneme yazın (240–280 kelime): İki metnin ana noktalarını mümkün olduğunca kendi sözlerinizle özetleyip değerlendirin ve kendi görüşünüzü ekleyin.\n\nText 1: \"Working from home has transformed the lives of millions of employees. Freed from long commutes, they enjoy more time with their families, greater control over their schedules and, in many cases, higher productivity.\"\n\nText 2: \"The shift to remote work comes at a hidden cost. Without the informal conversations of office life, younger employees miss out on vital learning opportunities, and many workers report feeling isolated and unable to switch off at the end of the day.\"",
          "The rapid growth of remote working has provoked considerable debate, and the two texts offer contrasting perspectives on its impact on employees.\n\nThe first text presents an overwhelmingly positive view. According to the writer, avoiding daily journeys to the office gives employees more family time and allows them to organise their working day as they wish. The writer also suggests that many people actually achieve more at home. These points are certainly valid, particularly for parents and for those who previously spent hours travelling. However, the claim about productivity is stated rather than supported, and the text ignores the possibility that the benefits may not be shared equally by all workers.\n\nThe second text, on the other hand, draws attention to less obvious disadvantages. The writer argues convincingly that the casual exchanges which happen naturally in an office play an important role in the development of less experienced staff. The text also highlights two widespread problems: loneliness and the difficulty of separating work from private life. In my view, the point about younger employees is particularly significant, since it suggests that the long-term cost of remote work may only become apparent years from now.\n\nOverall, I believe that both writers make reasonable points but present an incomplete picture. Remote work is clearly beneficial for many people, yet it is not suitable for everyone or for every stage of a career. A hybrid model, in which employees spend part of the week in the office, seems to me the most sensible way to combine the freedom described in the first text with the support and contact emphasised in the second.",
          ["Her iki metnin özeti", "Kendi sözleriyle ifade", "Eleştirel değerlendirme", "Net görüş", "Yapı ve kelime sınırı"]),
])

